  "scope": "Actual canonical read-only stdio MCP responses plus controlled external executable traces consumed by canonical verify/adapter parsers. Synthetic catalogs/bootstrap/traces are fixtures, not native harness discovery, installed-product checks, model sessions or whole E2E.",
  "problem": "Codex counted a completed MCP error response as successful invocation. Model adapters tested negative triggering using successful calls only, allowing failed/incomplete attempts to pass. Other result wrappers could admit errors or crash on absent/nonmapping responses.",
  "contracts": [
    "Only a nonempty mapping response without top-level isError/error or OMP details.isError/error proves successful invocation, with existing transport success checks retained.",
    "Explicit protocol or transport failure records INVOKED=FAIL when no successful call exists. Missing, malformed or incomplete results remain NOT_RUN.",
    "Track selected-tool attempts independently at start/use and terminal events. Negative verification rejects attempts even without a successful response.",
    "Native Hermes/OMP explicit response errors produce overall FAIL. Existing guide provenance, model loading and exit-status rules are unchanged."
  ],
